  "description": "DUDXAC crystallizes in the trigonal crystal system with space group P -3 1 c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C248 H168 La13 N54 O60 5+,C1 O3 2-,3(Cl1 1-),25(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, La1 (La) has 12 O neighbors; La2 (La) has 6 O neighbors; La3 (La) has 7 O neighbors; La2A (La) has 6 O neighbors; La2B (La) has 6 O neighbors; La2C (La) has 6 O neighbors; La2D (La) has 6 O neighbors; La2E (La) has 6 O neighbors; La3A (La) has 7 O neighbors; La3B (La) has 7 O neighbors; La3C (La) has 7 O neighbors; La3D (La) has 7 O neighbors; La3E (La) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 33 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 4.346-5.187 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 115.58-168.37°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula {[La13(H2O)6(phen)18(ccnm)6(CO3)14]·Cl3·CO3}·25(H2O). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 6 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
